      "text": "The default `AerSimulator` method is statevector, which doesn't record a unitary, so `result.get_unitary` fails. Setting `method='unitary'` makes the simulator build the unitary.\n\n```python\nfrom qiskit_aer import AerSimulator\nfrom qiskit import QuantumCircuit, transpile\n\ncirc = QuantumCircuit(2)\ncirc.h(0)\ncirc.cx(0, 1)\n\n# FIX: default AerSimulator method is statevector, which does not produce a unitary -> set method='unitary', because the unitary method is required for result.get_unitary to return the circuit's matrix\nsimulator = AerSimulator(method='unitary')\ncirc = transpile(circ, simulator)\n\nresult = simulator.run(circ).result()\nunitary = result.get_unitary(circ)\nprint(\"Circuit unitary:\\n\", unitary)\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
